Exceptions
==========

1. GPL-2.0: the spaceship pictures, derived from Vega Strike's ship models
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

These files are rendered from (or measured off) Vega Strike's ship meshes and
textures, and are licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 2,
as Vega Strike's art is.  (c) the Vega Strike contributors, and for the
rendering Daniel Reiter Horn.

The ships' sprite views, one file a ship type:

    art/ships/SHIP00.RV   Schroedinger (Vega Strike mesh Schroedinger/schroedinger.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP01.RV   Franklin (Vega Strike mesh Franklin/franklin.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP02.RV   Gawain (Vega Strike mesh Gawain/gawain.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP03.RV   Redeemer (Vega Strike mesh Redeemer/redeemer.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP04.RV   Pacifier (Vega Strike mesh Pacifier/pacifier.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP05.RV   Lancelot (Vega Strike mesh Lancelot/lancelot.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP06.RV   Progeny (Vega Strike mesh Progeny/progeny.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP08.RV   Nicander (Vega Strike mesh Nicander/nicander.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP09.RV   Ariston (Vega Strike mesh Ariston/ariston.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP0A.RV   Areus (Vega Strike mesh Areus/areus.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP0B.RV   Agis (built from parts of Vega Strike meshes (tools/hulls.py))
    art/ships/SHIP0C.RV   Cleomenes (built from parts of Vega Strike meshes (tools/hulls.py))
    art/ships/SHIP0D.RV   Convolution (Vega Strike mesh Convolution/convolution.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP10.RV   Shizu (Vega Strike mesh Shizu/shizu.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP11.RV   Zhuangzong (Vega Strike mesh Zhuangzong/zhuangzong.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP12.RV   Taizong (Vega Strike mesh Taizong/taizong.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP13.RV   Shizong (Vega Strike mesh Shizong/Shizong-Hi.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP14.RV   Xuanzong (Vega Strike mesh Xuanzong/Xuanzong.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP15.RV   Gaozong (Vega Strike mesh Gaozong/gaozong.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP20.RV   Vigilance (Vega Strike mesh Vigilance/vigilance.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP21.RV   Kahan (Vega Strike mesh Kahan/kahan.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP24.RV   Ox (Vega Strike mesh Ox/ox_new.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP25.RV   Goddard (Vega Strike mesh Goddard/goddard.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP28.RV   Agasicles (Vega Strike mesh Anaxidamus/anaxidamus.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP29.RV   Anaxidamus (Vega Strike mesh Anaxander/anaxander.obj)
    art/ships/SHIP2B.RV   Charillus (Vega Strike mesh Agasicles/agasicles.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP2C.RV   Leonidas (Vega Strike mesh Leonidas/yavok.bfxm)
    art/ships/SHIP30.RV   Ruizong (Vega Strike mesh Ruizong/ruizong.bfxm)

The fighters standing on the launch deck (art/places/deck/), each a render
of the ship's Vega Strike mesh:

    art/places/deck/ship-FRANKLN.png       art/places/deck/ship-FRANKLN-under.png
    art/places/deck/ship-GAWAIN.png        art/places/deck/ship-GAWAIN-under.png
    art/places/deck/ship-LANCELT.png       art/places/deck/ship-LANCELT-under.png
    art/places/deck/ship-PACIFER.png       art/places/deck/ship-PACIFER-under.png
    art/places/deck/ship-REDEEMR.png       art/places/deck/ship-REDEEMR-under.png
    art/places/deck/ship-SCHROED.png       art/places/deck/ship-SCHROED-under.png

Pictures of those ships in the documents:

    docs/aera-new.png
    docs/deck.png
    docs/franklin-liveries.png
    docs/franklin-sheet.png
    docs/gallery.png
    docs/packed.png
    docs/roster.png

The one piece of code ported from Vega Strike: the ship renderer's lighting,
a port of Vega Strike's uber shader (programs/uber.fp):

    tools/shipviews.py

The ships' sizes, collision shapes and engine points (data/shapes.dat,
data/hitboxes.csv, data/engines.csv, the sizes in data/ships.csv) are BSD
like the rest: the craft's sizes are RetroVega's own choice.  A game with
its own ships remakes them from its models with tools/hitboxes.py and
tools/engines.py.

Built files that contain the pictures above (RV.DAT, the ships' view files
.RVS/.RVH/.RV in the builds and on the web page) carry those pictures under
GPL-2.0 too; the rest of their content is BSD as above.


